{
	title: "Web never disturbs a reader's scroll or selection",
	spec: 'While Hal streams, a web reader keeps full control. The view never jumps: one glide chases the moving bottom and closes a fixed share of the distance each frame (scroll.tauMs), so new items, streamed lines and a send re-aim it without restarting it or setting the position at once. A reader more than 50 px above the bottom, or one who moves the view by wheel, touch, keys or the scrollbar, is left alone: the glide stops when scrollTop is not where it left it. A send ignores wheel momentum until its glide lands, at most scroll.forcedMs (300 ms). Rows once shown stay shown: the transcript pins its first shown row by key, so new rows only add below and never push old ones out of the DOM. No update moves the focus: effects that focus (Composer, Question) run behind memos that compare equal unless a form or picker opens or closes or the focused field changes. Invariants restored: no shown node is removed and no selection collapses while text streams; scrollTop changes only by the reader or by a glide toward the bottom for a reader at the bottom. Browser test in host/web.test.ts: a reader scrolled up with everything selected keeps the selection, the same nodes and scrollTop 0 while 80 rows stream.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Found with a headless Chrome test (Cmd+A, then 3 s of streaming). The Composer focus effect's compute returned a fresh boolean each update, yet its callback re-ran on every transcript change and called input.focus(), collapsing the selection within a second. In Solid 2 rc.11 a plain compute does not gate the effect; a createMemo does. The 40-row window (mfj) counted from the end, so each new row dropped the oldest from the DOM.",
		"A send's momentum hold that lasted until the glide landed held the view forever while a reply streamed (the bottom moves, so the glide never lands); the reader's wheel was ignored. Now a time limit, and landing clears it, else a later wheel within 300 ms is lost.",
		'Deleted flaky tests (AGENTS.md: delete, never retry): rotation edge gaps (web), and host tests that timed out at 5 s under full-suite load (turns, jobs, naming, history, host-transcript, host, turns-approval). Their behaviors are untested now.'
	],
